# DAYBOOK
## Complete Master Prompt – Production-Ready 3D Digital Personal Journaling Web Application

### PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a complete, production-ready web application called **Daybook**.

Daybook is a personal digital journaling application that recreates the experience of owning, organizing, and writing in real physical notebooks.

The central concept is to create a realistic digital personal study room where users can interact with physical-looking notebooks, a writing desk, a bookshelf, pens, erasers, photographs, bookmarks, and individual notebook pages.

Imagine a user entering their own peaceful study room.

There is a beautiful wooden table containing their active notebooks and a bookshelf containing their archived notebooks. They select a notebook, pick it up, open it, turn its pages, select a pen from a physical-looking pen box, write their thoughts, draw using a stylus, attach photographs, add bookmarks, and close the notebook when they finish.

The application should recreate this entire experience digitally.

**This is a WEB APPLICATION.** It must run in a browser and work across desktop computers, laptops, tablets, and mobile devices.

It is not a desktop-only application, a mobile-only application, or a static website.

Build the actual final product with working functionality, authentication, persistent cloud storage, realistic interactions, and a complete user experience.

Do not create a generic SaaS dashboard, productivity application, conventional note-taking website, or AI-generated website template.

The defining concept is:

**A personal digital study room containing realistic physical notebooks that users can pick up, open, write in, personalize, bookmark, organize, and archive.**

