# PART 2 — THE 3D STUDY ROOM

## 2.1 Main Environment

Create a beautiful, interactive 3D study room.

The room must contain two primary interactive objects:

1. A writing table.
2. A bookshelf.

Both objects must be recognizable as physical furniture and should be rendered with realistic proportions, materials, lighting, and shadows.

The user should be able to interact directly with these objects.

The room should feel like a personal study space rather than a game environment.

Do not add unnecessary characters, animated people, or distracting environmental objects.

## 2.2 First-Time User Experience

After signing in for the first time, introduce the user to their personal study room.

Show the room with its table and bookshelf.

The user should be able to:

- Click the table to view active notebooks.
- Click the bookshelf to view archived notebooks.
- Explore the room.
- Customize the furniture and environment.
- Create their first notebook.

Provide a simple introduction to the room without forcing users through a lengthy tutorial.

## 2.3 Regular User Experience

After the initial setup, the application must open directly into the **writing table view**.

Do not make users enter the full room and select the table every time.

The table should be the default home screen.

Users should immediately see their active notebooks and be able to select one.

Provide an easily accessible way to navigate to the bookshelf and return to the full room when desired.

## 2.4 Room Customization

Provide approximately 2–3 visually distinct options for each furniture category.

### Table styles

- Natural wooden writing desk.
- Dark polished wooden desk.
- Minimal elegant modern writing table.

### Bookshelf styles

- Classic wooden bookshelf.
- Dark traditional bookshelf.
- Minimal elegant bookshelf.

Each style must have its own realistic materials, appearance, and proportions.

Allow users to preview and select furniture styles.

Save their selections to their account.

Changing the table should not unexpectedly change the bookshelf or other application preferences.

