# PART 8 — LAST OPENED PAGE AND POSITION MEMORY

Implement automatic position memory for every notebook.

When users close a notebook or leave the application:

- Save the last opened page.
- Remember the user's position within the notebook.
- Save the last viewed date for Daily Journal notebooks.
- Preserve relevant notebook-specific writing preferences.
- Save the current editing state safely.

When users reopen the notebook, automatically return to where they stopped.

For Daily Journal notebooks, restore the last viewed journal date and corresponding entry.

Synchronize this information across devices.

If the user switches devices, prioritize the latest successfully synchronized state and avoid overwriting newer content with older data.

The user should never have to search for where they stopped writing.

