# PART 13 — PHOTOGRAPHS AND FREEFORM IMAGE PLACEMENT

Photographs should behave like actual printed pictures placed inside a physical notebook.

Allow users to:

- Upload photographs from their device.
- Drag and drop photographs directly onto a page.
- Move images freely anywhere.
- Resize using their corners.
- Rotate freely by grabbing and dragging an intuitive corner rotation handle.
- Overlap multiple photographs.
- Change their stacking order.
- Position images beside or between written content.
- Add multiple photographs to one page.

Do not require users to open a positioning menu or click a dedicated rotation button.

The interaction should be direct:

- Drag the photograph to move it.
- Grab its corners to resize it.
- Use an intuitive corner gesture to rotate it.
- Position it anywhere on the page.

Make photographs look like physical prints.

Optional visual details:

- White photo borders.
- Subtle shadows.
- Tape decorations.
- Slight natural rotations.

Preserve the exact position, dimensions, rotation, and layering of every photograph when saving and reopening a page.

Provide appropriate selection handles without leaving them permanently visible.

